{
    desc => q{A appends text at end of line},
    description => <<'END_DESC',
## Macro: `xt/visual/macros/insert_append_A`

Tests that the **A** command moves the cursor to the end of the current line
and enters insert mode, so typed text is appended to the end of the line.

**Keys:** `A`, type `!`, `Escape`

**initial.png**
- Buffer contains "Hello world"
- Cursor at column 0 on 'H'

**after_append_to_eol.png**
- Line reads "Hello world!" (exclamation appended at end)
- Cursor on '!' (moved back one after Escape)
END_DESC
    run => sub {
        my ($ctx) = @_;
        $ctx->buffer->set_text($CODE);
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->snapshot('initial');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->key('A');
        $ctx->type('!');
        $ctx->key('Escape');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->snapshot('after_append_to_eol');
    },
}
__DATA__
Hello world
